{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), we have almost no evidence about which design choices matter. The most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries meaningful signal at all, since RNA alone with PCA is barely above chance. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly tests this by holding profile setting constant (singleprofile) and using a standard, well-understood image encoder, making it a clean modality comparison against config_001. If image performs substantially better, the search should focus on image encoders and multimodal fusion; if it is also weak, the problem likely requires better RNA encoders or multimodal combination. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design axis (which modality is informative) before committing budget to more complex encoder, aggregation, or fusion choices."
}

